{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Between the evenings, a pesach to HaShem.</b> He mentioned the matter of the pesach even though its day is not a sacred convocation, because it is the cause of the variation in the times of the appointed festivals. For indeed, the fact that the intention was that the time of the pesach sacrifice for all generations be aligned with the time of that act of passing over — which took place at midnight of that same night — is the reason that this was entrusted to the court, their intercalation and calculation, as He explained in saying: שָׁמוֹר אֶת חֹדֶשׁ הָאָבִיב וְעָשִׂיתָ פֶּסַח לַה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ כִּי בְּחֹדֶשׁ הָאָבִיב הוֹצִיאֲךָ ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ מִמִּצְרַיִם לָיְלָה (Deuteronomy 16:1). And the tradition came regarding this, that they would fix the new moon of Pesach so that it would be in the spring."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:28.144309377Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}